<a href="mailto:prabhat.vaish@fedex.com">prabhat.vaish@fedex.com</a>; <a href="mailto:talib.ahmed@fedex.com">
talib.ahmed@fedex.com</a> ;<a href="mailto:surojit.biswas@fedex.com">surojit.biswas@fedex.com</a> with the subject line of the email as below
<o:p></o:p></p>
<p>Shipment Delivery Note- If shipment is cleared by consignee&#8217;s own CHA/Broker, delivery will be done by their appointed Broker. Fedex will not be responsible for delivery of the shipment irrespective of billing terms mentioned on AWB/Invoice copy.<o:p></o:p></p>
<p>Process to follow for Online DO collection as below <o:p></o:p></p>
<p>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;To release the online Delivery Order (DO), Please provide below details on&nbsp;
<a href="mailto:Deldo@corp.ds.fedex.com">Deldo@corp.ds.fedex.com</a> . <o:p></o:p></p>
<p><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; - Please provide authorization letter (in favor of Broker) from Consignee Official Email-ID. (Attached in the format)<o:p></o:p></p>
<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; - Kindly make the D.O Payment through NEFT mode of INR 3068/- on given FedEx Bank Account detail.&nbsp;(Refer Attachment)<o:p></o:p></p>
<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; - DO Payment clear editable details UTR/IMPS pasted on mail to : <a href="mailto:deldo@corp.ds.fedex.com">
deldo@corp.ds.fedex.com</a> <o:p></o:p></p>
